Section-wise Smart Questions (Strict BRD + Confirmation Logic)

⸻

1. Entry + Setup

1.1 “What is the use case name?”
1.2 “Is this a major change or minor change?”
1.3 “Please upload the BRD.”

⸻

2. BRD Analysis + Draft

2.1 “I’ve analyzed the BRD and identified key details (use case, sources, datasets, metrics, flow).”
2.2 “Here’s a summary — please confirm if this is correct before I proceed.”

👉 Rule: If user corrects → update before moving

⸻

3. Chapter Approval Status

3.1 Extract from BRD if available
3.2 If missing:
	•	“Please confirm the document producer name.”
	•	“Please provide the start date.”

👉 Do NOT proceed without these

⸻

4. Section 1 – Expected Outcomes (Scope)

4.1 Extract from BRD:
	•	Business objective
	•	Data usage
	•	Expected outcome

4.2 Generate 5–10 interpreted points

4.3 Ask:

“I’ve derived the scope based on the BRD — please confirm or suggest changes.”

👉 If BRD insufficient:

“Could you clarify the main objective of this use case?”

⸻

5. Section 2 – Metrics Summary

5.1 Extract:
	•	Metrics
	•	Source systems
	•	Categories

5.2 If partial:

“I found some metrics, but need more details — could you confirm or add missing ones?”

5.3 If missing:

“Please provide key metrics to include (5–6).”

5.4 Dashboards:
	•	If not in BRD:

“Do you want to include KPI or detailed dashboards?”

⸻

6. Section 3 – Logical Architecture

6.1 Extract:
	•	Source → EFDNA → Consumption flow

6.2 Generate diagram

6.3 Ask:

“I’ve mapped the logical architecture — please confirm if this flow is correct.”

👉 If unclear:

“Could you confirm the flow between source and consumption?”

⸻

7. Section 3.1 – Data Management

7.1 Extract ALL columns from BRD:
	•	Dataset
	•	Source
	•	Volume
	•	Retention
	•	Frequency
	•	Data model

7.2 For EACH missing field:

“I couldn’t find [field] — could you provide it?”

7.3 After filling:

“Please confirm the data management details.”

⸻

8. Section 3.2 – Data Flow Diagram

8.1 Generate from BRD

8.2 Ask:

“I’ve created the data flow diagram — please confirm if this matches the process.”

⸻

9. Section 3.3 – Data Completeness Checklist

9.1 Read requirement row-by-row

9.2 Infer:
	•	YES / NO / NA

9.3 If uncertain:

“For [capability], should this be marked as YES or NO?”

9.4 Ask once:

“Please confirm the checklist responses.”

⸻

10. Section 4 – Integration

10.1 Extract:
	•	Source systems
	•	Data movement

10.2 Infer:
	•	Mechanism (JDBC/ODBC/API/File)
	•	Type (Batch/Online)
	•	Frequency

10.3 Ask:

“I’ve identified integration as [mechanism + batch/online + frequency] — please confirm.”

10.4 If missing:

“Could you confirm the integration mechanism and frequency?”

10.5 Sensitive data:

Ask ONLY if unclear

⸻

11. Section 5 – Technologies Adopted

11.1 Extract:
	•	Application
	•	Tools
	•	Storage

11.2 Infer:
	•	Technology components
	•	Impact = NEW

11.3 Ask:

“I’ve mapped the technology stack — please confirm.”

11.4 If missing:

“Could you provide missing technology details like CMDB/GTS ID?”

⸻

12. Section 6 – Security Architecture

12.1 Analyze:
	•	Data sensitivity
	•	Changes in system

12.2 Fill checklist

12.3 Ask:

“I’ve completed the security checklist based on BRD — please confirm.”

12.4 If unclear:

“Is this considered a new application or enhancement?”

⸻

13. Section 7 – Cloud Checklist

13.1 Check BRD

13.2 If missing:

“Is this solution deployed on cloud? If yes, which model (SaaS/IaaS/PaaS/Hybrid)?”

13.3 Confirm:

“Please confirm the cloud setup details.”

⸻

14. Section 8 – Application Impact

14.1 Infer:
	•	Functional changes
	•	Integration impact
	•	Performance

14.2 Ask:

“I’ve assessed the application impact — please confirm if this is correct.”

⸻

15. Section 9 – Architecture Significance

15.1 Infer all YES/NO

15.2 Ask:

“I’ve evaluated architectural significance — please confirm.”

⸻

16. Section 10 – Standards Alignment

16.1 Infer:
	•	Technology principles
	•	Data principles
	•	Security

16.2 Ask:

“I’ve aligned this solution with relevant standards — please confirm or modify.”

⸻

17. Final Draft Step

17.1 “I’ve prepared a complete draft of all sections.”
17.2 “Would you like me to generate the final document?”
